Propellerhead Remote Mapping File
File Format Version	1.0.0
Control Surface Manufacturer	Akai
Control Surface Model	MPK Mini Play
Map Version	1.0.0


//======================================================================
//  Radical Keys
//
//  Pads      -> reserved (patch & effect toggle templates below)
//  Knobs 1-4A-> tone / blend / response / master   (CC21-24)
//  Knobs 1-4B-> envelope & compressor               (CC25-28)
//  Joystick X-> Pitch Bend
//  Joystick Y-> (no Mod Wheel remotable; see below)
//  Keyboard  -> Keyboard
//
//  NOTE: Scope is se.propellerheads.RadicalKeys (CamelCase) - the
//  Rack Extension device ID as Reason reports it. Remote item names
//  (mic1, mic2, Instrument Blend, Vel Resp Curve etc.) follow the
//  Reason Remote template for this device.
//======================================================================

Scope	Propellerhead Software	se.propellerheads.RadicalKeys
// Define Group	Keyboard Shortcut Variations	Tone	Env
//	Control Surface Item	Key	Remotable Item	Scale	Mode

Map	_Scope		"Radical Keys"
Map	Keyboard		Keyboard

// --- Pads (reserved) ---------------------------------
// Radical Keys has no drum pads; ready-to-enable templates:
// Map Pad 1		Select Previous Patch
// Map Pad 2		Select Next Patch
// Map Pad 3		Overdrive OnOff
// Map Pad 4		Comp OnOff
// Map Pad 5		Tremolo OnOff
// Map Pad 6		Chorus OnOff
// Map Pad 7		Phaser OnOff
// Map Pad 8		Ambience OnOff

// --- Knob Bank A (CC21-24): tone & blend ------------
Map	Knob 1 A		Character
Map	Knob 2 A		Instrument Blend
Map	Knob 3 A		Vel Resp Curve
Map	Knob 4 A		Master Volume

// --- Knob Bank B (CC25-28): envelope & dynamics -----
Map	Knob 1 B		Env Attack
Map	Knob 2 B		Env Decay Curve
Map	Knob 3 B		Env Release
Map	Knob 4 B		Comp Amount

// --- Joystick / wheels -------------------------------
Map	Joystick X		Pitch Bend
// Radical Keys responds to Pitch Bend and Sustain Pedal but exposes
// no Mod Wheel remotable. Use a Remote Override to re-point the Y axis
// to a continuous destination such as Ambience Level if desired:
//Map	Joystick Y		Ambience Level